\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Motivation.} Consider the \texttt  {Graph} coloring problem shown in \textbf  {A} (left), with six valid solutions. We evaluate Qwen2.5-3B across training, tracking the number and diversity of correct solutions. At each training pass, we show 32 sampled questions, eight from each of four matched runs. Training with Dr. GRPO (\textbf  {B}) improves accuracy and leads to a single solution dominating the output. In contrast, Re:Max (\textbf  {C}) increases both accuracy and diversity of correct solutions. }}{1}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
