\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {12}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Replay outperforms KL anchoring.} Means over five domains for Qwen2.5-0.5B. The anchor forms a curve because we sweep several $\beta $-KL coefficients. Increasing $\beta $ preserves more solution diversity, but at a lower \texttt  {pass@8}. Green indicates where an arm achieves higher \texttt  {pass@8} than the anchor at the same level of diversity (App.\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {app:theory-kl-measured}).}}{9}{figure.45}\protected@file@percent }
