\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {\textsc  {ModeBench}{} provides executable solution identities across five domains.} Correctness and identity come from one validator; training starts without the mode catalogue. \emph  {Valid modes} gives the mean and range of certified catalogue counts over the released Level-1 evaluation split. These counts need not exhaust all outputs accepted by the verifier; \texttt  {Countdown} permits valid keys outside its enumerated catalogue. \emph  {Reached} is mean distinct verified modes from one hosted deployment at 512{} draws on 32{} problems per domain (Fig.\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {fig:gpt56-sampling-budget}), selected independently of outputs from that split. The columns use the full evaluation split and its sampling subset, respectively. \texttt  {MathIR}'s catalogue includes longer derivations; low observed coverage does not distinguish inaccessible routes from rare routes missed at these sampling budgets. Higher levels have separate constructions and support distributions (App.\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {app:data-levels}). App.\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {app:prompts} gives the prompts and chat templates.}}{22}{table.75}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:tasks}{{3}{22}{\textbf {\mb {} provides executable solution identities across five domains.} Correctness and identity come from one validator; training starts without the mode catalogue. \emph {Valid modes} gives the mean and range of certified catalogue counts over the released Level-1 evaluation split. These counts need not exhaust all outputs accepted by the verifier; \texttt {Countdown} permits valid keys outside its enumerated catalogue. \emph {Reached} is mean distinct verified modes from one hosted deployment at \MDreachedDraws {} draws on \MDreachedPrompts {} problems per domain (Fig.~\ref {fig:gpt56-sampling-budget}), selected independently of outputs from that split. The columns use the full evaluation split and its sampling subset, respectively. \texttt {MathIR}'s catalogue includes longer derivations; low observed coverage does not distinguish inaccessible routes from rare routes missed at these sampling budgets. Higher levels have separate constructions and support distributions (App.~\ref {app:data-levels}). App.~\ref {app:prompts} gives the prompts and chat templates}{table.75}{}}
