\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {18}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Replay raises mean correctness at all three model scales.} Terminal Re:Dr minus Dr.GRPO (circles) and Re:Max minus MaxRL (squares). The axes show percentage-point changes in \texttt  {pass@8} and changes in \texttt  {PCMD}{}. Filled marks use five paired seeds; open marks use fewer. For Re:Dr, correctness uses four seeds in Falcon \texttt  {Countdown}; diversity uses four in Falcon \texttt  {Countdown}, one in Falcon \texttt  {MathIR}, and two in Qwen2.5-3B \texttt  {Python}. Blank cells have no eligible comparison. Diversity requires at least 20 defining prompts per arm. Bars are nominal paired 95\% Student-$t$ intervals, requiring five seeds for correctness and at least two for diversity.}}{34}{figure.142}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:replay-factorial-effects}{{18}{34}{\textbf {Replay raises mean correctness at all three model scales.} Terminal Re:Dr minus Dr.GRPO (circles) and Re:Max minus MaxRL (squares). The axes show percentage-point changes in \texttt {pass@8} and changes in \pmd {}. Filled marks use five paired seeds; open marks use fewer. For Re:Dr, correctness uses four seeds in Falcon \texttt {Countdown}; diversity uses four in Falcon \texttt {Countdown}, one in Falcon \texttt {MathIR}, and two in Qwen2.5-3B \texttt {Python}. Blank cells have no eligible comparison. Diversity requires at least 20 defining prompts per arm. Bars are nominal paired 95\% Student-$t$ intervals, requiring five seeds for correctness and at least two for diversity}{figure.142}{}}
