\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {23}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Removing \texttt  {Python} guidance reduces correctness and observed breadth.} Local Qwen2.5-0.5B checkpoints under strict verification, with original $\to $ neutral wording. $P_8=\texttt  {pass@8}$, $D_8=\texttt  {distinct@8}$, and $B_8=D_8-P_8$ use eight draws on each of 32 problems per domain and level. Effects are neutral minus original. $P_8$, $D_8$, and $B_8$ average the displayed number $s$ of checkpoints. Brackets are pointwise 95\% bootstrap intervals: paired problems and training seeds are resampled for five-seed groups; \texttt  {Pantry} intervals condition on its two checkpoints, and initial-model intervals on one checkpoint. \texttt  {PCMD}{} is the mean probability that two verified draws on a problem differ, pooled over checkpoint--problem groups with at least two verified draws in each arm. Its paired population depends on correctness, and repeated problems at different checkpoints count separately. Only 5 of 18 cells meet the minimum of 30 such groups; dashes denote the others. \texttt  {PCMD}{} has no reported interval.}}{56}{table.232}\protected@file@percent }
